---@class posthog.vision.CreateVisionScannersDraftRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field goal string What the user wants to accomplish, e.g. 'find out where users get stuck during onboarding'.
---@field monthly_credit_budget? number Credits a month to spend (1 credit = $0.01). The draft picks the `model`, then solves `sampling_mode` and `sampling_rate` so the projected spend lands on this number, and sets `credit_limit` to it as a hard cap. Ask the person for it rather than guessing. Required unless `free_only` is true, and not allowed with it.
---@field free_only? boolean Draft a scanner that runs only on the organization's free monthly credits, so it never adds to the bill and pauses when they run out. The draft is sized to those free credits and comes back with `free_only` true and no `credit_limit`. Use instead of `monthly_credit_budget`.
---@field experiment_id? number A launched experiment the person picked for the scanner to watch. The draft is then an `experiment` scanner on it.
---@field query? any A `RecordingsQuery` the person already chose, as the replay list holds it. The draft starts from it and never removes or widens it. When the goal asks for narrower recordings, the draft can AND its own page, event, action or cohort filters onto it. It keeps them only when the combined filter still matches recent recordings, returns them in `query_additions`, and sizes the sampling dials against the combined `query`. `experiment_exposure` becomes the scanner's experiment and variants, which the draft keeps as they are. `date_from`/`date_to` are dropped, because a scanner's schedule owns time. `comment_text`, `hide_viewed_recordings` and in-session exposure are refused, because a scanner cannot apply them. A query with no filters starts from every new recording. Omit to let the draft pick the sessions.

---@class posthog.vision.CreateVisionScannersEstimateRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field query? any Proposed `RecordingsQuery` for the candidate filter. `date_from`/`date_to` are ignored — the estimate scans a recent window (`window_days` in the response) and scales it to 30 days. Omit to estimate against all recordings.
---@field sampling_rate? number 0..1 downsample applied to matched sessions. Defaults to 1.0 (no downsampling).
---@field sampling_mode? posthog.vision.SamplingModeEnum|string Quality pre-filter applied to the matched-session count, mirroring the sweep's candidate query. Defaults to comprehensive (no filter). * `focused` - Focused * `balanced` - Balanced * `comprehensive` - Comprehensive
---@field scanner_id? string|distilled.Null The scanner being edited, excluded from `other_enabled_scanners_monthly_credits` so its stored estimate isn't double-counted in the forecast. Omit (or null) when estimating a brand-new scanner.
---@field model? posthog.vision.ScannerModelEnum|string Proposed model; determines `credits_per_observation` in the response. * `gemini-3.5-flash-lite` - Gemini 3.5 Flash Lite * `gemini-3-flash-preview` - Gemini 3 Flash * `gemini-3.8-flash` - Gemini 3.8 Flash
---@field experiment_targeting? posthog.vision.ScannerExperimentTargeting|distilled.Null Proposed experiment targeting, merged into the query as its exposure filter the same way a saved scanner derives it. The estimate then runs as the requesting user.
---@field experiment? posthog.vision.EstimateExperimentScope|distilled.Null For an experiment scanner: the `experiment_id` and `variants` it will keep in its config, merged into the query as its exposure filter so the estimate counts only exposed sessions. Not combined with `experiment_targeting`.

