---@field display_name? string Name shown wherever people identify this scout, written however you want it — spaces, capitalization, and acronyms are kept as typed, and two scouts may share one. It does not change the scout's skill name, which stays its identity, so renaming a scout keeps its schedule, run history, notes, memory, and links. At most 200 characters; blank means the scout has no name of its own and is labelled from its skill name instead.
---@field name? string Optional skill name for the scout — its permanent identifier, containing only lowercase letters, numbers, and hyphens. Omit it and one is generated from `display_name` (`My APM scout` becomes `my-apm-scout`), with a numeric suffix when that name is taken. Pass it to pick the identifier yourself, or to keep a client written before display names working unchanged. The `signals-scout-` prefix is optional.
---@field description string Short description of the signal or behavior this scout investigates.
---@field body string Complete markdown prompt executed on every scout run. Include any project-specific signal names, thresholds, investigation steps, and report criteria here.
---@field config? posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigOptions Optional schedule, enablement, dry-run posture, and delivery settings. Defaults to an enabled, emitting scout on the daily interval with no external destination.
---@field variant_analysis? boolean Make this the experiment scanner's variant analysis scout: its runs record a structured comparison of the variants, which the scanner's variants readout shows. Experiment scanners only.
---@field template_key? posthog.vision.ScoutTemplateKeyEnum|string The template the body came from. A body left exactly as the template rendered it keeps following later edits to that template; an edited body stays as written. * `variant-analysis` - Variant analysis * `daily-digest` - Daily digest * `root-cause` - Root cause * `weekly-themes` - Weekly themes * `trend-watch` - Trend watch * `new-issues` - New issue watch * `scratch` - Start from scratch

---An AI-drafted scanner configuration, ready to seed the creation wizard. Nothing is persisted.
---@class posthog.vision.DraftScannerResponse
---@field name string Drafted scanner name.
---@field description string Drafted one-sentence description.
---@field scanner_type posthog.vision.ScannerTypeEnum The scanner type the draft picked for the goal. * `monitor` - Monitor * `classifier` - Classifier * `scorer` - Scorer * `summarizer` - Summarizer * `experiment` - Experiment
---@field scanner_config any Type-specific config for the drafted `scanner_type`; always includes `prompt`.
---@field rationale string Why the draft picked this scanner type and configuration, addressed to the user.
---@field query any `RecordingsQuery` narrowing which sessions get scanned; null when the draft targets every session.
---@field query_additions any When the request passed a `query`: the filters the draft ANDed onto it, which `query` already includes. Show them to the person as added by AI. Null when nothing was added or no `query` was passed.
---@field sampling_mode posthog.vision.SamplingModeEnum|distilled.Null The quality pre-filter the draft chose for the goal. Null when the costing estimate failed, in which case the wizard keeps its defaults. * `focused` - Focused * `balanced` - Balanced * `comprehensive` - Comprehensive
---@field sampling_rate number|distilled.Null The random sampling rate solved from `monthly_credit_budget`, 0..1. 1.0 when the budget covers every matching recording. Floored at the minimum rate, so a budget below that floor keeps the minimum. Null whenever `sampling_mode` is.
---@field model posthog.vision.ScannerModelEnum|distilled.Null The observation model the draft chose for the goal, by how much judgment it needs. * `gemini-3.5-flash-lite` - Gemini 3.5 Flash Lite * `gemini-3-flash-preview` - Gemini 3 Flash * `gemini-3.8-flash` - Gemini 3.8 Flash
---@field credit_limit number|distilled.Null The monthly credit cap, set to `monthly_credit_budget` so a mis-estimate stops the scanner at the credits the user agreed to. Null for a free-only draft.
---@field free_only boolean Whether the draft runs only on the organization's free monthly credits. Pass it on to create.
---@field estimated_monthly_observations number|distilled.Null Recordings a month the drafted scanner is projected to watch under the solved dials. Its credit cost lands at or under `monthly_credit_budget`, except when the budget is below what the minimum sampling rate can reach, where this is the floor and exceeds the budget. Null whenever `sampling_mode` is.

---@class posthog.vision.EstimateExperimentScope
---@field experiment_id number The experiment an experiment scanner watches.
---@field variants? posthog.vision.EstimateExperimentScopeVariantsList|distilled.Null The variant keys it watches. Null or omitted means every variant.

---The variant keys it watches. Null or omitted means every variant.
---@alias posthog.vision.EstimateExperimentScopeVariantsList string[]

---Forward-looking volume and credit-cost estimate for a proposed scanner.
---@class posthog.vision.EstimateResponse
---@field matched_sessions_in_window number Distinct sessions matching the query within the scanned window (`window_days`), after the sampling_mode quality filter but before random sampling.
---@field window_days number Days of recordings the estimate scanned before scaling to 30. Up to a week (shorter when the query's operand rules out sampling); smaller when the team has fewer days of recordings.
---@field estimated_observations_per_month number Projected monthly observations: quality-filtered matched sessions scaled from `window_days` to 30 days, times sampling_rate.
---@field credits_per_observation number Credits one observation costs at the proposed `model` (1 credit = $0.01).
---@field estimated_credits_per_month number `estimated_observations_per_month` priced at `credits_per_observation`.
---@field other_enabled_scanners_monthly_credits number Credit-weighted projected monthly spend of the org's other enabled scanners (excluding `scanner_id`), from their cached estimates. Read from the same snapshot as this estimate so the forecast can't double-count the edited scanner.
---@field active_backfill_credits number Committed-but-unspent credits of the org's active backfills, the same figure the quota snapshot's projection carries. A one-off charge rather than a monthly rate, so the forecast shows it as its own segment instead of adding it to a per-month total.
---@field free_only_monthly_credits_left number The monthly credit rate the organization's free credits still cover for one more free-only scanner, after the other free-only scanners and backfills. The forecast caps a free-only scanner at this rate, because free-only scanners share one pool.
---@field sampling_rate number Sampling rate applied to the projection. Echoed from the request.

