---@class posthog.vision.GetVisionGroupRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id string
---@field by_variant? boolean Split each group's window counts by experiment variant in `variants`. Use it on experiment scanners.
---@field date_from? string Count members from this time: ISO 8601 or relative like `-7d`. Defaults to `-30d`. The window spans at most 90 days with `scanner_id`, and at most 30 days without it.
---@field date_to? string Count members up to this time: ISO 8601, relative, or `now`. Defaults to now.
---@field include_routine? boolean Also count routine observations, so groups describe ordinary behavior and not only issues. Use it for experiment scanners, where the question is how each variant's users behave.
---@field scanner_id? string Only this scanner's clusters. Defaults to every scanner you can read.
---@field variant? string Experiment scanners only: count only members attributed to these variant keys (comma-separated). `__unattributed__` matches members with no attributed variant.

---@class posthog.vision.GetVisionObservationRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id string A UUID string identifying this replay observation.
---@field backfill_id? string Only observations dispatched by this backfill.
---@field date_from? string Only observations created at or after this time. Accepts ISO 8601, a relative date like `-7d`, or `now`; values without an explicit offset are interpreted in the project's timezone.
---@field date_to? string Only observations created at or before this time. Accepts ISO 8601, a relative date like `-1d`, or `now` for the current time; omit it to query through the current time. Date-only values include the whole day, interpreted in the project's timezone.
---@field group? string Only issue observations in this group of near duplicates, an `id` from the groups list. Pair it with the same `date_from`, `date_to`, `include_routine` and `variant` to list the observations the group counted.
---@field include_routine? boolean With `group`, also list the group's routine observations, as the groups list does with the same flag.
---@field labeled? boolean When true, return only observations that have a shared label (thumbs up or down); when false, only unlabeled observations.
---@field max_score? number Filter scorer observations to those scoring at or below this value. Rows with no numeric score (other scanner types, failed or in-flight runs) are excluded.
---@field min_score? number Filter scorer observations to those scoring at or above this value. Rows with no numeric score (other scanner types, failed or in-flight runs) are excluded.
---@field order_by? posthog.vision.GetVisionObservationRequestOrderBy|string Sort observations. Plain keys: created_at, started_at, completed_at, status, recording_subject_email. JSONB keys: result_score (scorer), result_verdict (monitor), result_confidence, scanner_version. Prefix with `-` for descending; nullable keys sort nulls last either way.
---@field recording_subject? string Filter to observations whose person email contains this value (case-insensitive).
---@field session_id? string Filter to observations of one or more session recordings. Accepts a comma-separated list.
---@field status? string Filter by observation status. Accepts a comma-separated list.
---@field tags? string Filter classifier observations whose fixed or freeform tags include any of the given values (comma-separated). Matches if the tag appears in either `tags` or `tags_freeform`.
---@field theme? string Only issue observations in this search theme, an `id` from the themes list. Pair it with the same `date_from` and `date_to` to list the observations the theme counted.
---@field triggered_by? string Filter by trigger source (schedule, on_demand, retry, or backfill). Accepts a comma-separated list.
---@field variant? string Experiment scanners only: filter to observations attributed to any of the given variant keys (comma-separated). `__unattributed__` matches observations with no attributed variant.
---@field verdict? string Filter monitor observations by verdict. Accepts a comma-separated list (e.g. `yes,inconclusive`).
---@field watch_category? string Only observations the watch feed ranks under any of these kinds (comma-separated: failure, struggle, revenue). Pair it with `watch_group` and the feed's `categories`.
---@field watch_group? string Only observations the highlight feed groups with this observation as near duplicates, including itself. Pair it with the feed's `date_from` to list the sessions a feed card counts.

---@alias posthog.vision.GetVisionObservationRequestOrderBy "-completed_at"|"-created_at"|"-label"|"-recording_subject_email"|"-result_confidence"|"-result_score"|"-result_verdict"|"-scanner_version"|"-started_at"|"-status"|"completed_at"|"created_at"|"label"|"recording_subject_email"|"result_confidence"|"result_score"|"result_verdict"|"scanner_version"|"started_at"|"status"

