---@class posthog.vision.GetVisionScannersHighlightFeedRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field as_of? string The time the first page loaded. Later pages rank as of that time: observations, views, dismissals and impressions after it are ignored, so pages do not shift under a reader who scrolls.
---@field categories? string Comma-separated kinds of moment to include: `failure` (errors, failed requests, dead ends), `struggle` (repeated attempts, rage clicks, abandoned forms), `revenue` (failed payments, cancellations, usage limits). Defaults to all three. A pick keeps its rank within its scanner, so leaving a kind out drops its sessions without promoting weaker ones.
---@field created_by? string Comma-separated user IDs. Restrict the feed to observations from scanners those users created.
---@field date_from? string Only observations created at or after this time. Accepts ISO 8601, a relative date like `-7d`, or `now`; values without an explicit offset are interpreted in the project's timezone. The window between `date_from` and `date_to` may span at most 90 days.
---@field date_to? string Only observations created at or before this time. Same formats as `date_from`; omit it to query through the current time.
---@field limit? number Ceiling on feed items to return per page, at most 50. A page routinely returns fewer: a window is not padded to this number with clips that carry no finding.
---@field offset? number How many ranked items to skip. Send `as_of` with every page after the first.
---@field scanner_ids? string Comma-separated scanner UUIDs to restrict the feed to. Defaults to every scanner you can read.
---@field scanner_type? posthog.vision.GetVisionScannersHighlightFeedRequestScannerType|string Restrict the feed to observations from scanners of this type. * `monitor` - Monitor * `classifier` - Classifier * `scorer` - Scorer * `summarizer` - Summarizer * `experiment` - Experiment
---@field tags? string Comma-separated scanner tags to restrict the feed to. A team with many scanners uses these to follow one area without naming every scanner in it.

---@alias posthog.vision.GetVisionScannersHighlightFeedRequestScannerType "monitor"|"classifier"|"scorer"|"summarizer"|"experiment"

