---Response of GET /vision/scanners/highlight_feed/.
---@class posthog.vision.HighlightFeedResponse
---@field results posthog.vision.HighlightFeedResponseResultsList Succeeded observations in the window worth watching, most interesting first, each carrying the reason it ranked. Every observation that carries a finding is returned; observations that carry none (`unviewed_recent`, `recent`) are returned only to pad a near-empty feed to three items, so a quiet window answers with a handful of rows rather than a full page of newest clips.
---@field has_more boolean Whether a later page holds more ranked items. Request it with `offset` set past this page.
---@field as_of string The time this feed ranks as of. Send it back with later pages.

---Succeeded observations in the window worth watching, most interesting first, each carrying the reason it ranked. Every observation that carries a finding is returned; observations that carry none (`unviewed_recent`, `recent`) are returned only to pad a near-empty feed to three items, so a quiet window answers with a handful of rows rather than a full page of newest clips.
---@alias posthog.vision.HighlightFeedResponseResultsList posthog.vision.HighlightFeedItem[]

---A question asked inline, without saving a scanner first.
---@class posthog.vision.InlineScanConfig
---@field built_in? posthog.vision.BuiltInScanKeyEnum|string Run a scan PostHog defines instead of your own prompt. `summarize_recording` is the AI summary the Summarize button in the replay player runs, so its results are shared with that button. Leave out `prompt`, `scanner_type` and `scanner_config` when this is set. * `summarize_recording` - Summarize recording
---@field prompt? string What to look for in these sessions, in plain language. The same instruction a saved scanner carries. Required unless `built_in` is set.
---@field scanner_type? posthog.vision.ScannerTypeEnum|string What the scan produces. Defaults to monitor, an open-ended observation against the prompt. Use `summarizer` for a summary in your own words; use `built_in: summarize_recording` for the Summarize button's summary. An inline scan is keyed by its whole config, so asking the same question again reuses its answers. * `monitor` - Monitor * `classifier` - Classifier * `scorer` - Scorer * `summarizer` - Summarizer * `experiment` - Experiment
---@field scanner_config? any Type-specific configuration beyond the prompt: `tags` for a classifier, `scale` for a scorer, optional `length` for a summarizer. Omit it for a monitor. `prompt` belongs in the `prompt` field and is rejected here.
---@field model? posthog.vision.ScannerModelEnum|string Model to scan with. Determines what each observation costs in credits. * `gemini-3.5-flash-lite` - Gemini 3.5 Flash Lite * `gemini-3-flash-preview` - Gemini 3 Flash * `gemini-3.8-flash` - Gemini 3.8 Flash

