---@field session_id? string Filter to observations of one or more session recordings. Accepts a comma-separated list.
---@field status? string Filter by observation status. Accepts a comma-separated list.
---@field tags? string Filter classifier observations whose fixed or freeform tags include any of the given values (comma-separated). Matches if the tag appears in either `tags` or `tags_freeform`.
---@field theme? string Only issue observations in this search theme, an `id` from the themes list. Pair it with the same `date_from` and `date_to` to list the observations the theme counted.
---@field triggered_by? string Filter by trigger source (schedule, on_demand, retry, or backfill). Accepts a comma-separated list.
---@field variant? string Experiment scanners only: filter to observations attributed to any of the given variant keys (comma-separated). `__unattributed__` matches observations with no attributed variant.
---@field verdict? string Filter monitor observations by verdict. Accepts a comma-separated list (e.g. `yes,inconclusive`).
---@field watch_category? string Only observations the watch feed ranks under any of these kinds (comma-separated: failure, struggle, revenue). Pair it with `watch_group` and the feed's `categories`.
---@field watch_group? string Only observations the highlight feed groups with this observation as near duplicates, including itself. Pair it with the feed's `date_from` to list the sessions a feed card counts.

