---@alias posthog.vision.PaginatedVisionAlertEventListResultsList posthog.vision.VisionAlertEvent[]

---@alias posthog.vision.PromptValenceEnum "good"|"bad"|"neutral"

---@class posthog.vision.ReplayObservation
---@field id string
---@field scanner_id string The scanner that produced this observation.
---@field scanner_origin posthog.vision.ScannerOriginEnum Where the producing scanner came from. `configured` scanners are saved, named, and have a detail page; `inline` ones are throwaways minted for a one-off scan and are not addressable, so callers must not link to them. * `configured` - Configured * `inline` - Inline
---@field session_id string Session recording id this scanner was applied to.
---@field status posthog.vision.ObservationStatusEnum Observation status (pending, running, succeeded, failed, ineligible). * `pending` - Pending * `running` - Running * `succeeded` - Succeeded * `failed` - Failed * `ineligible` - Ineligible
---@field error_reason string Populated on terminal non-success statuses; formatted as `kind:human-readable message`. For `ineligible`, kind is one of no_recording / too_short / too_inactive / too_long / no_events / no_snapshots / too_large / not_exposed / experiment_unresolved. For `failed`, kind is one of provider_transient / provider_rejected / rasterization_failed / validation_failed / infra_transient / internal_error / orphaned / pii_detected.
---@field workflow_id string Temporal workflow id for progress queries and debugging. Empty until the workflow starts.
---@field scanner_snapshot posthog.vision.ScannerSnapshot|distilled.Null Frozen view of the scanner at run time; scanner edits do not retroactively mutate this observation.
---@field scanner_result posthog.vision.ScannerResult|distilled.Null Result data persisted on success; null until the observation succeeds.
---@field prompt_question string|distilled.Null The scanner's prompt condensed into the one question it answers about a session. Null when the prompt has changed since this observation was scanned, since the question then describes a different prompt; read `scanner_snapshot.scanner_config.prompt` instead.
---@field prompt_valence posthog.vision.PromptValenceEnum|distilled.Null For a monitor or scorer: `good` when a yes or a high score is good news for the team, `bad` when it is a problem, `neutral` when neither. Judged by AI from the prompt. Null for other scanner types, when not judged, or when the prompt has changed since this observation was scanned.
---@field triggered_by posthog.vision.ObservationTriggerEnum Whether this observation came from the schedule, an on-demand request, a retry of a failed or ineligible observation, or a historical backfill. * `schedule` - Schedule * `on_demand` - On demand * `retry` - Retry * `backfill` - Backfill
---@field triggered_by_user posthog.vision.UserBasic|distilled.Null User who triggered an on-demand observation; null for scheduled observations.
---@field backfill_id string|distilled.Null Backfill that dispatched this observation; null for live, on-demand, and retry triggers.
---@field distinct_id string|distilled.Null Distinct id of the person in the recorded session (the subject being watched); null if unknown.
---@field recording_subject_email string|distilled.Null Email of the person in the recorded session (the subject being watched, not the user who triggered the observation), captured at scan time. Null when the session had no identified person.
---@field previous_observation_id string|distilled.Null Id of the preceding sibling observation for the same scanner (prev/next nav), honoring any list filters and ordering passed to retrieve; only set on retrieve, null at the start of the set.
---@field next_observation_id string|distilled.Null Id of the following sibling observation for the same scanner (prev/next nav), honoring any list filters and ordering passed to retrieve; only set on retrieve, null at the end of the set.
---@field label posthog.vision.ReplayObservationLabel|distilled.Null The team's shared label on this observation (correct/incorrect + feedback), or null if unlabeled.
---@field viewed boolean Whether the calling user has opened this observation.
---@field media posthog.vision.ReplayObservationMediaList Frames illustrating this observation, in order. Empty until the media render finishes.
---@field summary_line string One line of plain text saying what the scanner found: its verdict, score, tags or title, then its own words, with markdown flattened and the text truncated. An observation that produced no result carries the reason instead, and one still in flight carries an empty string. Read this in place of `scanner_result` when you scan a list of observations.
---@field started_at? string|distilled.Null
---@field completed_at? string|distilled.Null
---@field created_at string

---The team's shared judgement on whether the scanner scored this session correctly.
---@class posthog.vision.ReplayObservationLabel
---@field is_correct boolean True if the scanner scored this session correctly, false if not.
---@field feedback? string Optional written context on the rating, for thumbs-up and thumbs-down alike: what the scanner got right or wrong, or what it should have concluded.

---One frame illustrating an observation.
---@class posthog.vision.ReplayObservationMedia
---@field id string Id of this media entry.
---@field kind posthog.vision.ReplayObservationMediaKindEnum `thumbnail` for the single frame that illustrates the observation, `chapter` for the frame of one summary chapter. * `thumbnail` - Thumbnail * `chapter` - Chapter
---@field position number Order among media of the same kind. For a `chapter` frame, the index into `model_output.chapters`.
---@field asset_id number Export asset holding the bytes; fetch it from the export content endpoint.
---@field video_start_ms number Where this media starts in the analysis video, in milliseconds.

---* `thumbnail` - Thumbnail
---* `chapter` - Chapter
---@alias posthog.vision.ReplayObservationMediaKindEnum "thumbnail"|"chapter"

---Frames illustrating this observation, in order. Empty until the media render finishes.
---@alias posthog.vision.ReplayObservationMediaList posthog.vision.ReplayObservationMedia[]

---@class posthog.vision.ReplayScannerBackfill
---@field id string
---@field status posthog.vision.BackfillStatusEnum
---@field window_start string Inclusive lower bound of the historical window to scan.
---@field window_end string Exclusive upper bound of the window; clamped to now at creation.
---@field total_count number Unobserved candidates enumerated at creation; the ceiling is total_count x credits_per_observation.
---@field dispatched_count number
---@field skipped_count number Candidates the walk stepped over because this scanner had already tried them. Counted at creation but never dispatched, so progress and remaining spend both have to account for them.
---@field credits_per_observation number Per-observation credit price frozen at creation from the snapshot model.
---@field succeeded_count number Observations from this backfill that succeeded.
---@field failed_count number Observations from this backfill that failed.
---@field ineligible_count number Sessions that turned out ineligible (too short, expired recording, ...).
---@field in_flight_count number Observations from this backfill still pending or running.
---@field created_by posthog.vision.UserBasic|distilled.Null
---@field created_at string
---@field finished_at string|distilled.Null When the backfill reached a terminal status (completed or cancelled).

---A Replay Vision scanner: its type, targeting query, and AI configuration.
---@class posthog.vision.ReplayScannerOutput
---@field id string
---@field name string Human-readable scanner name. Unique within the team.
---@field description? string Free-form description shown in the scanner management UI.
---@field tags? posthog.vision.ReplayScannerOutputTagsList Organizational tags for this scanner. Distinct from a classifier's categories in scanner_config. Tags cannot contain commas.
---@field scanner_type posthog.vision.ScannerTypeEnum What the scanner does: monitor, classifier, scorer, or summarizer. * `monitor` - Monitor * `classifier` - Classifier * `scorer` - Scorer * `summarizer` - Summarizer * `experiment` - Experiment
---@field goal? string|distilled.Null The goal an AI draft was built from, in the creator's own words, so the scanner keeps what it was meant to find. Set on create only and ignored on update.
---@field scanner_config any Type-specific configuration. All scanner types require `prompt`; monitors add optional `allow_inconclusive`, classifiers add `tags`, scorers add `scale`, summarizers add optional `length`.
---@field prompt_question string The current prompt condensed by AI into the one question the scanner answers about a session. Falls back to the prompt's first line when no question matches the current prompt.
---@field query? any Persisted `RecordingsQuery` shape used to pick candidate sessions. `date_from`/`date_to` are stripped on save — the schedule controls time, not the user.
---@field sampling_rate? number 0..1 random downsample applied after the query matches. Defaults to 1.0 (no downsampling). Use exactly 0 to pause scanning; non-zero rates below 0.0001 (0.01%) are rejected as below the sampling precision.
---@field sampling_mode? posthog.vision.SamplingModeEnum Quality pre-filter applied before random sampling. focused = top sessions only, balanced = drops the lowest-quality, comprehensive = no filter (default). * `focused` - Focused * `balanced` - Balanced * `comprehensive` - Comprehensive
---@field credit_limit? number|distilled.Null Optional cap on this scanner's own credit spend per billing period. Null means no scanner-level cap. When reached, this scanner stops scanning until the period resets. It stays enabled and does not scan the sessions it skipped.
---@field free_only? boolean Run only while the organization has free credits left this billing period, so the scanner never adds spend.
---@field provider? posthog.vision.ScannerProviderEnum LLM provider. v1 is Google-only. * `google` - Google
---@field model posthog.vision.ScannerModelEnum Concrete model to use for this scanner. * `gemini-3.5-flash-lite` - Gemini 3.5 Flash Lite * `gemini-3-flash-preview` - Gemini 3 Flash * `gemini-3.8-flash` - Gemini 3.8 Flash
---@field enabled? boolean When false, the reconciler removes the scanner's Temporal schedule. On-demand triggers still work.
---@field emits_signals? boolean When true, the prompt is augmented with the Signal side mission and the scanner emits PostHog Signals.
---@field experiment_targeting? posthog.vision.ScannerExperimentTargeting|distilled.Null The experiment this scanner's targeting watches, if any. Set null when the experiment targeting is removed.
---@field scanner_version number Increments on every config-changing save. Observations snapshot this value.
---@field estimated_monthly_observations number|distilled.Null Latest projected observations/month for this scanner. Null until first computed.
---@field estimated_at string|distilled.Null When `estimated_monthly_observations` was last computed. Null means the estimate is being recomputed after a config change or has never run, so the stored number may be stale.
---@field credits_per_observation number Credits one observation by this scanner costs (1 credit = $0.01), derived from `model`.
---@field estimated_monthly_credits number|distilled.Null `estimated_monthly_observations` priced at `credits_per_observation`, capped at `credit_limit` when one is set. Null until the estimate is first computed.
---@field credits_this_month number Credits billed for this scanner's observations created in the current billing period (1 credit = $0.01), each at the price frozen when it succeeded. Deleted observations still count.
---@field observations_this_month number Billed observations this scanner created in the current billing period, including deleted ones.
---@field credits_used_against_limit number Credits counted against `credit_limit` for the current billing period: settled receipts plus in-flight observations, priced from their frozen snapshot model. This is what the limit gate measures, so it includes work still in progress. It is not the same as `credits_this_month`, which counts only succeeded observations. For a `free_only` scanner bound by the organization's free credits, this is the organization's usage, not the scanner's own.
---@field limit_from_free_credits boolean True when the organization's free credits bind this `free_only` scanner rather than its own `credit_limit`. `credits_used_against_limit` is then the organization's usage, measured against its free credits.
---@field limit_reached boolean Whether this scanner has stopped because of its own credit limit, or, for a `free_only` scanner, because the organization has used its free credits. True when the budget left cannot cover one more observation, which is the same test the scanner's enforcement gates apply. Always false when no limit is set and `free_only` is false.
---@field sweep_throttle_factor number How much the scheduled sweep is slowed to keep this scanner inside its daily ClickHouse read budget. 1 means it checks for new recordings on the normal schedule; N means it checks once every N schedule intervals. Expensive filters raise it.
---@field dashboard_id number|distilled.Null Dashboard created for this scanner with the create_dashboard action. Null when none was created or the user deleted it.
---@field dashboard_suggested boolean Whether to offer the user a dashboard for this scanner: true when the scanner has no dashboard and at least 20 succeeded observations to chart. Offer it once and do not repeat the offer if the user declines.
---@field last_swept_at string Watermark for the scanner's last scheduled fire. Mirrors Temporal schedule state for recovery.
---@field filter_error string|distilled.Null Why the scanner's recording filter cannot run, from the last sweep or estimate that tried it. Cleared when the filter changes or a sweep runs it.
---@field unrunnable_reason posthog.vision.UnrunnableReasonEnum|distilled.Null Why the scanner can never run, or null when it can. `no_ai_consent`: the organization has not approved AI data processing. `creator_lost_access`: the creator can no longer view recordings, which the sweep reads as them, so turning the scanner on requires `take_over_as_creator`. The sweep turns an enabled scanner off when either applies.
---@field created_at string
---@field created_by posthog.vision.UserBasic|distilled.Null User who created the scanner.
---@field updated_at string
---@field user_access_level string|distilled.Null The effective access level the user has for this object

---Organizational tags for this scanner. Distinct from a classifier's categories in scanner_config. Tags cannot contain commas.
