---@field title string|distilled.Null Report title. Null until the report is summarized.
---@field status string The report's inbox status.

---Read shape for a per-(team, skill) scout config.
---
---One row per scout skill on the team. The coordinator auto-creates a row
---when it discovers a scout skill; this serializer lets agents tune the row.
---@class posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfig
---@field id string
---@field skill_name string The skill this config controls as a scout. Set at creation, not editable.
---@field description string Human-readable summary of what this scout investigates, sourced from the scout skill's `description` metadata. Use it for a quick steer on the scout's focus without loading the full skill body. Empty if the skill is not currently present on the team or carries no description.
---@field display_name? string Name shown in the UI. Does not change the skill name. Leave blank to use the default name.
---@field scout_origin posthog.vision.ScoutOriginEnum Where this scout came from: `canonical` for a scout PostHog ships and maintains (seeded from `products/signals/skills/`), or `custom` for one a team hand-authored on this project. Use it to badge built-in vs custom scouts instead of a hardcoded name list. Defaults to `custom` if the skill is not currently present on the team.
---@field scout_role posthog.vision.ScoutRoleEnum What this scout is to the harness: `specialist` for one that watches a product surface, or `operational` for one PostHog ships to watch the self-driving system itself. An operational scout is exempt from the inactivity sweep and from the enabled-scout cap, and is not a scout a project should delete. Always `specialist` for a custom scout.
---@field deprecation posthog.vision.ScoutDeprecation|distilled.Null Set when PostHog is retiring this scout, and null otherwise. Carries the phase, the reason to show, what replaces the scout, and when it stops running. Only a canonical scout the project has not edited is ever marked: a project's own copy keeps running and reads as null.
---@field owners posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigOwnersList Who answers for this scout, seed-creator first. Ownership is recorded on the scout's skill rather than on this config, so editing the skill or toggling the scout leaves it unchanged. Reports the scout files suggest these people as reviewers. Prefer this over `created_by`-style fields, which only say who last flipped a switch. Empty when nobody owns the scout, when the owners are no longer members with access to the project, or when the caller is a scout sandbox token: owners are member PII, and a scout reads them through the skill API instead.
---@field enabled boolean Whether this scout runs on its schedule. Disabled scouts are skipped by the coordinator. Derived from `status`: true for `active` and `pending_pause`, false for the paused statuses.
---@field status posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigStatusEnum Lifecycle status. `active`: runs on its schedule. `pending_pause`: still running, but flagged by the system to pause soon unless something changes (any config edit clears it). `paused_by_system`: paused automatically, see `pause_reason`; set `enabled=true` to resume. `paused_by_user`: switched off by a person and never resumed automatically. * `active` - Active * `pending_pause` - Pending pause * `paused_by_system` - Paused by system * `paused_by_user` - Paused by user
---@field pause_reason posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigPauseReasonEnum|distilled.Null Why the system paused (or warned) this scout: `no_output` (it emitted nothing over the evaluation window), `ignored` (no person engaged with its reports — no view, rating, note, dismissal, or resolution), `repeated_failures` (consecutive failed runs), `retired` (PostHog retired the scout), or `background_removed` (the background lane stopped managing the scout). Null unless `status` is `pending_pause` or `paused_by_system`. * `no_output` - No output * `ignored` - Ignored * `repeated_failures` - Repeated failures * `retired` - Retired * `background_removed` - Background removed
---@field managed_by posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigManagedByEnum Who controls this scout now. `team`: a person set it up or has changed it. `background`: PostHog runs it in the background and no person has edited it yet. Any edit through this API changes `background` to `team`. * `team` - Team * `background` - Background
---@field emit boolean Whether the scout writes findings to the inbox. False = dry-run: it runs and logs but emits nothing.
---@field run_interval_minutes number Minutes between runs (30–43200). The scout runs once this interval has elapsed since its last run.
---@field run_cron_schedule string|distilled.Null Optional five-field cron expression evaluated in the project timezone, e.g. '30 9 * * *'. Takes precedence over `run_interval_minutes` when set. Null means the rolling interval schedule.
---@field output_destinations posthog.vision.SignalScoutOutputDestinations Destinations that receive each finding or report this scout emits. Empty when none is configured.
---@field structured_output_schema posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigStructuredOutputSchemaMap|distilled.Null Optional JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) describing ONE structured record this scout produces via `scout-record-output` — e.g. a per-report quality judgment (`{"type": "object", "properties": {"verdict": {"enum": ["good", "bad", "unsure"]}, "reason": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["verdict", "reason"]}`). The root must be `"type": "object"`. Setting a schema turns the structured-output channel on: the run prompt renders the schema and every submitted record is validated against it and recorded in the project as a `$scout_structured_output` event, queryable like any event. The channel also requires emit — a dry-run scout has nowhere to record to. Cardinality is the scout's call (one record per run, one per judged entity, ...). Null = channel off. Setting a schema requires skill-authoring authorization (the `llm_skill:write` scope and skill editor access) since the scout reads it verbatim in its prompt; clearing it needs only the config write. Records validate against the schema in force when the run was dispatched.
---@field network_access posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigNetworkAccessEnum What the scout's sandbox can reach over the network while it runs. `trusted` (the default) restricts runs to the platform's trusted-domain allowlist (PostHog, GitHub, common package registries). `full` lets the scout reach any site, for skills that read external sources such as documentation or papers. * `trusted` - Trusted domains only * `full` - Full
---@field model string|distilled.Null Optional model id this scout's runs are pinned to, e.g. `claude-opus-4-5`. Must be one of the platform's agent models; an invalid id is rejected with the available ones listed. Null keeps the default model, chosen by the platform. Early access: the pin can only be set on projects enrolled in the scout model preview, and only takes effect there. Set null to clear it.
---@field mcp_gateway_server_ids posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigMcpGatewayServerIdsList MCP gateway servers (by id) this scout's runs may use, chosen from the connections members shared to the whole team. Selection is per scout: an empty list gives the scout no MCP servers. Applies from the scout's next run.
---@field repositories? posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigRepositoriesList GitHub repositories this scout clones into its sandbox, each in `organization/repo` format. Set them for a scout that reads code, so it can search the tree and run the project's own tests instead of reading files one API call at a time. Empty (the default) leaves the sandbox without a checkout. The scout's GitHub access stays read-only either way, so a repository listed here is never writable from a run. At most 10, each reachable through the project's GitHub connection. Applies from the scout's next run.
---@field write_scopes posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigWriteScopesList Write access granted to this one scout, as scope strings. The grantable set is `alert:write`, `annotation:write`, `canvas:write`, `customer_task:write`, `dashboard:write`, `event_definition:write`, `experiment:write`, `hog_flow_proposal:write`, `insight:write`, `llm_skill:write`, `notebook:write`, `replay_scanner:write`, `ticket:write`, `warehouse_table:write`, `warehouse_view:write`. A new scout starts with `notebook:write` when this field is omitted. Empty means the scout reads the project and writes only its findings and its own memory. Each scope is project-wide and object-level, so a scout holding `dashboard:write` can update or delete any dashboard in the project, not only ones it made. `ticket:write` lets the scout update tickets, manage saved views, and add private notes. Scouts cannot send public replies, compose emails, change existing notes, or change customer identity fields. Ticket changes can start workflows that message customers. `event_definition:write` lets the scout change the tags on event definitions and nothing else. Grant only what this scout maintains. Only the person the scout's runs act as (whoever authored it) or a project admin can set it, and a scoped API key must itself carry each scope it grants. A dry run (`emit=false`) never holds the grant, and a run that acts as a project member other than the author holds only the default scopes. Applies from the scout's next run.
---@field lifecycle_locked boolean Opt-in guard on this scout's lifecycle. Off by default, so anyone with scout write access may pause, resume, switch the scout to dry run, or delete it. On, only the person the scout's runs act as or a project admin may do any of those, or change this flag. Use it on a scout whose output people depend on: `signal_scout:write` is a project-wide scope held by people and by unattended agents alike, and a resume has to pass the project's enabled-scout maximum that a pause does not, so a bulk pause is not undone in one step. The lock never stops an automatic pause, such as the inactivity sweep or the repeated-failure breaker.
---@field allowed_mcp_tools posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigAllowedMcpToolsList|distilled.Null Exact MCP tool names selected for this scout, excluding its built-in run context tools. Null means no tool restriction; an empty list selects no additional tools. Write access is derived from selected write tools. Clearing to null preserves the last write scopes. Send this field or tool_preset, never both. Requires the scouts-tool-access feature flag.
---@field tool_preset string|distilled.Null Preset used to select the saved tool list, custom for an explicit list, or null when unrestricted.
---@field precheck_query string|distilled.Null Optional HogQL `SELECT` a scheduled run evaluates before it starts. When it returns no rows, or one row with one false value (`false`, `0`, null or empty), the run is skipped: no sandbox, no model call, and no run row. Any other result starts the run, and the scout reads the rows. A query error also starts the run. Use `{since}` (the start of the last run that ran, or when the scout was created) and `{now}` to look only at what is new, e.g. `SELECT count() FROM events WHERE event = '$exception' AND timestamp > {since}`. To run at least once a week however quiet it is, add `OR {since} < {now} - INTERVAL 7 DAY` to the condition. Only scheduled runs evaluate it: a manual or workflow run always starts. `{interval_minutes}` is the gap between two scheduled runs, so a backstop can follow the schedule: `{since} < {now} - toIntervalMinute(greatest(1440, 2 * {interval_minutes}))` runs at least daily and never more often than every two intervals. The query stops after 10 seconds and reads at most 50 rows. Try a query with `scout-config-precheck-test` before you save it. Null or blank uses the default pre-check the scout's skill ships, if any. To turn every pre-check off, set `precheck_disabled`.
---@field precheck_disabled boolean True turns off the pre-check, both `precheck_query` and the default the skill ships, so every scheduled run starts. False (the default) uses `precheck_query`, or the skill default when that is null.
---@field effective_precheck_query string|distilled.Null The pre-check query the next scheduled run uses: `precheck_query`, or the default the scout's skill ships. Null when no pre-check runs.
---@field precheck_query_source posthog.vision.ScoutPrecheckQuerySourceEnum Where `effective_precheck_query` comes from: `config` (this scout's `precheck_query`), `skill_default` (the default its skill ships), or `off` (no pre-check runs).
---@field last_precheck_at string|distilled.Null When a scheduled run last evaluated this scout's pre-check. A skipped run writes no run row, so this stays recent while `last_run_at` ages. Null if no pre-check has run.
---@field last_precheck_outcome posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigPrecheckOutcomeEnum|distilled.Null The outcome of the latest scheduled pre-check: `run` (the query found something new), `skip` (nothing new, so the run did not start), or `error` (the query failed and the run started). Null if no pre-check has run. * `run` - Run * `skip` - Skip * `error` - Error
---@field last_precheck_row_count number|distilled.Null How many rows the latest scheduled pre-check returned, at most 50. Null if no pre-check has run.
---@field last_run_at string|distilled.Null When the coordinator last dispatched this scout. Null if it has never run.
---@field consecutive_failure_count number How many of this scout's runs have failed in a row. Back to 0 after a successful run or any config edit. At the failure limit the scout pauses itself (`status` becomes `paused_by_system` with `pause_reason` `repeated_failures`) and retries about once a day; a successful retry resumes it, and so does setting `enabled=true`.
---@field status_changed_at string|distilled.Null When `status` last changed. For `pending_pause` this is when the warning was issued (an `ignored` warning pauses about a week later unless someone engages with the scout's reports — opening one counts; a `no_output` warning only flags the scout); for the paused statuses it is when the scout was paused. Null if the status never changed.
---@field status_changed_by posthog.vision.UserBasic|distilled.Null Who last moved `status`, when a person did it through this API. Null for a system transition such as an automatic pause, for a row whose status never changed, and for a caller that may not read member identities. Pair it with `status` to say who turned a scout off, instead of only when it went off.
---@field auto_pause_exempt boolean Whether this scout is exempt from the inactivity sweep, meaning both the `ignored` pause and the `no_output` quiet warning. Set it on watchdog scouts whose value is staying quiet. Only ever set explicitly: re-enabling a swept scout instead grants a fresh grace window before the sweep may judge it again.
---@field tags? posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigTagsList Free-form labels for grouping the fleet, e.g. `["revenue", "on-call"]`. Normalized to lowercase kebab-case (`On Call` and `on_call` both become `on-call`), deduped, and stored sorted; at most 10 tags, each at most 50 characters once normalized. Pass the full desired set — a write replaces the existing tags rather than merging into them. Filter the config list with the `tags` query parameter.
---@field source_product string|distilled.Null The product that stood this scout up for one of its own objects. Null when a person created it.
---@field source_id string|distilled.Null Id of the owning object in `source_product`, e.g. a Replay Vision scanner id.
---@field created_at string
---@field updated_at string When this config last changed: an edit through this API, or a status change the system made such as an automatic pause. A scheduled run does not bump it — the coordinator stamps `last_run_at` with a direct write — so this reads as when the scout was last tuned rather than when it last ran.

---Exact MCP tool names selected for this scout, excluding its built-in run context tools. Null means no tool restriction; an empty list selects no additional tools. Write access is derived from selected write tools. Clearing to null preserves the last write scopes. Send this field or tool_preset, never both. Requires the scouts-tool-access feature flag.
---@alias posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigAllowedMcpToolsList string[]

---* `team` - Team
---* `background` - Background
---@alias posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigManagedByEnum "team"|"background"

---MCP gateway servers (by id) this scout's runs may use, chosen from the connections members shared to the whole team. Selection is per scout: an empty list gives the scout no MCP servers. Applies from the scout's next run.
---@alias posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigMcpGatewayServerIdsList string[]

---* `trusted` - Trusted domains only
---* `full` - Full
---@alias posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigNetworkAccessEnum "trusted"|"full"

