---Optional JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) describing ONE structured record this scout produces via `scout-record-output` — e.g. a per-report quality judgment (`{"type": "object", "properties": {"verdict": {"enum": ["good", "bad", "unsure"]}, "reason": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["verdict", "reason"]}`). The root must be `"type": "object"`. Setting a schema turns the structured-output channel on: the run prompt renders the schema and every submitted record is validated against it and recorded in the project as a `$scout_structured_output` event, queryable like any event. The channel also requires emit — a dry-run scout has nowhere to record to. Cardinality is the scout's call (one record per run, one per judged entity, ...). Null = channel off. Setting a schema requires skill-authoring authorization (the `llm_skill:write` scope and skill editor access) since the scout reads it verbatim in its prompt; clearing it needs only the config write. Records validate against the schema in force when the run was dispatched.
---@alias posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigStructuredOutputSchemaMap { [string]: any }

---Free-form labels for grouping the fleet, e.g. `["revenue", "on-call"]`. Normalized to lowercase kebab-case (`On Call` and `on_call` both become `on-call`), deduped, and stored sorted; at most 10 tags, each at most 50 characters once normalized. Pass the full desired set — a write replaces the existing tags rather than merging into them. Filter the config list with the `tags` query parameter.
---@alias posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigTagsList string[]

---Write access granted to this one scout, as scope strings. The grantable set is `alert:write`, `annotation:write`, `canvas:write`, `customer_task:write`, `dashboard:write`, `event_definition:write`, `experiment:write`, `hog_flow_proposal:write`, `insight:write`, `llm_skill:write`, `notebook:write`, `replay_scanner:write`, `ticket:write`, `warehouse_table:write`, `warehouse_view:write`. A new scout starts with `notebook:write` when this field is omitted. Empty means the scout reads the project and writes only its findings and its own memory. Each scope is project-wide and object-level, so a scout holding `dashboard:write` can update or delete any dashboard in the project, not only ones it made. `ticket:write` lets the scout update tickets, manage saved views, and add private notes. Scouts cannot send public replies, compose emails, change existing notes, or change customer identity fields. Ticket changes can start workflows that message customers. `event_definition:write` lets the scout change the tags on event definitions and nothing else. Grant only what this scout maintains. Only the person the scout's runs act as (whoever authored it) or a project admin can set it, and a scoped API key must itself carry each scope it grants. A dry run (`emit=false`) never holds the grant, and a run that acts as a project member other than the author holds only the default scopes. Applies from the scout's next run.
---@alias posthog.vision.SignalScoutConfigWriteScopesList string[]

---@class posthog.vision.SignalScoutOutputDestinations
---@field slack? posthog.vision.SignalScoutSlackDestination|distilled.Null Slack destination for each emitted scout finding or report. Null or omitted disables Slack delivery.
---@field webhook? posthog.vision.SignalScoutWebhookDestination|distilled.Null The CDP destination another product provisioned for this scout's reports. Null or omitted means no webhook. Unlike Slack, Signals does not deliver this itself: the reference lives here so the owning product can manage the destination's lifecycle.
---@field inbox? boolean Whether this scout's reports appear in the shared inbox. Defaults to true. Set false to keep the reports this scout authors out of the inbox and its Slack notifications, for example for a digest scout read in Slack. Reports this scout only edits are not affected. An update that omits this key keeps the stored value.

---@class posthog.vision.SignalScoutSlackDestination
---@field integration_id number ID of the Slack integration whose bot posts this scout's findings and reports.
---@field channel? string|distilled.Null Slack channel target in the channel picker's `channel_id|#channel-name` format. Null while choosing a channel; no messages are sent until a channel or user is set.
---@field users? posthog.vision.SignalScoutSlackDestinationUsersList|distilled.Null Slack members to send output to as direct messages, each in `member_id|@display-name` format (a bare member ID like `U0123ABC456` also works). Each member gets their own DM from the PostHog app; at most 5. Set either this or `channel`, not both. Useful for personal scouts where a DM beats a channel.
---@field thread_reports? boolean When true, post a report as a thread: a short lead in the channel and the rest split into replies at the summary's section labels, which can be Markdown headings or bold labels. Keeps a long summary from being clipped at Slack's section limit. On by default; set it false to post a single message, which can truncate a long summary. It does not change how findings post.

---Slack members to send output to as direct messages, each in `member_id|@display-name` format (a bare member ID like `U0123ABC456` also works). Each member gets their own DM from the PostHog app; at most 5. Set either this or `channel`, not both. Useful for personal scouts where a DM beats a channel.
---@alias posthog.vision.SignalScoutSlackDestinationUsersList string[]

