---@class posthog.vision.UpdateVisionScannersPartialRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id string A UUID string identifying this replay scanner.
---@field name? string Human-readable scanner name. Unique within the team.
---@field description? string Free-form description shown in the scanner management UI.
---@field tags? posthog.vision.UpdateVisionScannersPartialRequestTagsList Organizational tags for this scanner. Distinct from a classifier's categories in scanner_config. Tags cannot contain commas.
---@field scanner_type? posthog.vision.ScannerTypeEnum|string What the scanner does: monitor, classifier, scorer, or summarizer. * `monitor` - Monitor * `classifier` - Classifier * `scorer` - Scorer * `summarizer` - Summarizer * `experiment` - Experiment
---@field goal? string|distilled.Null The goal an AI draft was built from, in the creator's own words, so the scanner keeps what it was meant to find. Set on create only and ignored on update.
---@field creation_method? posthog.vision.ScannerCreationMethodEnum|string|distilled.Null How the creator built this scanner: from an AI draft, from a template, or from scratch. Reported to product analytics at creation and not stored on the scanner. Independent of any experiment the creator is in, since a person offered the AI flow can still fill the form by hand. Only the app can answer this, so a request from anywhere else reports the calling surface instead of whatever it sends here. Ignored on update. * `ai` - AI draft * `template` - Template * `scratch` - From scratch
---@field entry_point? string|distilled.Null The app surface the creator started from, such as `replay_filters`. Reported to product analytics at creation so a scanner can be attributed to its entry point, and not stored on the scanner. Only the app's value is kept: any other caller is reported as its own source, such as `mcp`. Ignored on update.
---@field take_over_as_creator? boolean Set with `enabled: true` to turn on a scanner whose creator can no longer view recordings. The caller becomes the scanner's creator, and scheduled scans then run as the caller. Without it, that request fails with code `scanner_creator_lost_access`.
---@field scanner_config? any Type-specific configuration. All scanner types require `prompt`; monitors add optional `allow_inconclusive`, classifiers add `tags`, scorers add `scale`, summarizers add optional `length`.
---@field query? any Persisted `RecordingsQuery` shape used to pick candidate sessions. `date_from`/`date_to` are stripped on save — the schedule controls time, not the user.
---@field sampling_rate? number 0..1 random downsample applied after the query matches. Defaults to 1.0 (no downsampling). Use exactly 0 to pause scanning; non-zero rates below 0.0001 (0.01%) are rejected as below the sampling precision.
---@field sampling_mode? posthog.vision.SamplingModeEnum|string Quality pre-filter applied before random sampling. focused = top sessions only, balanced = drops the lowest-quality, comprehensive = no filter (default). * `focused` - Focused * `balanced` - Balanced * `comprehensive` - Comprehensive
---@field credit_limit? number|distilled.Null Optional cap on this scanner's own credit spend per billing period. Null means no scanner-level cap. When reached, this scanner stops scanning until the period resets. It stays enabled and does not scan the sessions it skipped.
---@field free_only? boolean Run only while the organization has free credits left this billing period, so the scanner never adds spend.
---@field provider? posthog.vision.ScannerProviderEnum|string LLM provider. v1 is Google-only. * `google` - Google
---@field model? posthog.vision.ScannerModelEnum|string Concrete model to use for this scanner. * `gemini-3.5-flash-lite` - Gemini 3.5 Flash Lite * `gemini-3-flash-preview` - Gemini 3 Flash * `gemini-3.8-flash` - Gemini 3.8 Flash
---@field enabled? boolean When false, the reconciler removes the scanner's Temporal schedule. On-demand triggers still work.
---@field emits_signals? boolean When true, the prompt is augmented with the Signal side mission and the scanner emits PostHog Signals.
---@field experiment_targeting? posthog.vision.ScannerExperimentTargeting|distilled.Null The experiment this scanner's targeting watches, if any. Set null when the experiment targeting is removed.

---Organizational tags for this scanner. Distinct from a classifier's categories in scanner_config. Tags cannot contain commas.
